// Project Image. L7, COPY-ONLY per this school's scope decision: builds only
// the illusory-copy half (a stationary phantasm double that spawns near the
// caster). The remote-viewpoint half (seeing/hearing through it at range,
// moving it independently of the caster) is a different, not-yet-built
// mechanism and is deliberately absent here -- this double does not move on
// its own, is not piloted, and carries no sensing wiring.
//
// Scope note (body): the source spell's double is shaped exactly like the
// caster. `SummonInfo::Npc.body` is a single value fixed at asset-load time,
// with no way for a RON to say "copy whatever body summoned me" -- that
// would need new Rust to substitute the caster's own `Body` into the summon
// at cast time (the character-state code already has `data.body` in scope,
// see `common/src/states/basic_summon.rs`, so it is a small addition, but
// still a Rust change and out of scope for this pure-content pass).
// `Object(TrainingDummy)` -- a still, human-shaped decoy figure -- stands in
// as the closest honest data-only silhouette; it is not a likeness of the
// specific caster.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.5,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: Object(TrainingDummy),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        // Matches the compendium entry's Concentration(60) cap.
        duration: Some((
            secs: 60,
            nanos: 0,
        )),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
